## Conceptual Contributions

### Asymmetric Error Tolerance as an Evaluation Criterion
The use of role-differentiated error tolerance thresholds — rather than single-standard accuracy metrics — as a core AI evaluation criterion in operational deployment contexts.

### Linguistic Dimension of Prompt Quality
The explicit identification of multilingual workforce dynamics as a structural variable in Store-Level AI evaluation — distinct from general prompt quality variance and requiring separate measurement.

### Somatic State as AI Interaction Variable
The application of somatic intelligence concepts (Gilligan Generative Coaching framework) and neurological levels (Dilts) to the design and evaluation of human-AI interaction in operational retail environments.  
*Developed in Article 2B.*

### GRADE Radar as Evaluation Output
The five-dimensional radar visualization as a standardized output format for Store-Level AI evaluation — enabling dimension-level diagnosis rather than aggregate accuracy reporting.

